{"name":"Laredo","hex":"#d79a74","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Laredo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large city, the county seat of Webb County, Texas, United States.","A city in north Tamaulipas, Mexico."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Laredo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laredo, Spain","blocks":[{"text":"Laredo is a town in the autonomous community of Cantabria, Spain. According to the 2008 census (INE), the municipality has a population of 12,648 inhabitants. In addition to Laredo, the municipality includes the villages of La Arenosa, El Callejo, Las Cárcobas, Las Casillas, La Pesquera, Tarrueza and Villante. Except from the last two, the other villages had been physically integrated into Laredo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Laredo.jpg/330px-Laredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laredo%2C_Spain","wikidata":"Q828955"},{"title":"Laredo District","blocks":[{"text":"Laredo District is one of eleven districts of the Trujillo Province in the La Libertad region, Peru."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/OvaloLaredo.JPG/330px-OvaloLaredo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laredo_District","wikidata":"Q5390290"},{"title":"Laredo (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Laredo is an American Western television series that aired on NBC from 1965 to 1967, starring Neville Brand, William Smith, Peter Brown, and Philip Carey as Texas Rangers. It is set on the Mexican border around Laredo in Webb County in South Texas. The program presented 56 episodes in color. It was produced by Universal Television. The series has a comic element, but like another NBC series that premiered in 1965, The Wackiest Ship in the Army, it was an hour in length, had no laugh track, and characters were frequently killed, thus going against three unofficial rules for sitcoms at the time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/10/Laredo_%28TV_series%29.png/330px-Laredo_%28TV_series%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laredo_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q941025"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Antiguopuertolaredo.jpg/120px-Antiguopuertolaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Antiguopuertolaredo.jpg/250px-Antiguopuertolaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Antiguopuertolaredo.jpg/120px-Antiguopuertolaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntiguopuertolaredo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Murallalaredo.jpg/120px-Murallalaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Murallalaredo.jpg/250px-Murallalaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Murallalaredo.jpg/120px-Murallalaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMurallalaredo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Iglesialaredo.jpg/120px-Iglesialaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Iglesialaredo.jpg/250px-Iglesialaredo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi